diff -ruN a/debian/NEWS b/debian/NEWS
--- a/debian/NEWS
+++ b/debian/NEWS
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+valkey (9.0.7-3) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  freshdeb: on arm64, valkey-server now also runs on kernels with 16K or
+  64K pages (Raspberry Pi 5, Asahi Linux, Ubuntu's -64k kernels), where it
+  used to abort with "<jemalloc>: Unsupported system page size". Its bundled
+  jemalloc is now built for 64K pages, as Debian's libjemalloc is; on 4K
+  kernels that can use a little more memory.
+
+ -- freshdeb <packages@freshdeb.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
